{
    "background_story": "Theodora was a remarkable lungfish belonging to the ancient family Ceratodontidae. She lived in the murky waters of a prehistoric lake, where the air was thick with humidity and the vegetation was lush. Theodora's species had evolved to thrive in this environment, developing lungs to breathe air from the surface. As the lake's water levels fluctuated, Theodora would burrow into the mud, using her powerful fins to excavate a cozy nest. Her ability to survive out of water for short periods made her a curious creature, often exploring the lake's edges and discovering hidden treasures. Theodora's unique adaptations and resilience allowed her to thrive in a world where few others could, earning her a special place in the ancient ecosystem.",
